From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:22:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] core: union table wildcards and withsource

- Wildcarded table names (union Device*) failed with "Name group is not in
  scope": Kusto.Language binds them to a GroupSymbol of the matching tables.
  Each member now becomes its own union input.
- withsource=Col produced an empty column. Every input now carries its source
  name: the table name for a table reference (wildcard members included),
  union_arg<position> for any other expression (a subquery, or the piped
  input), as Kusto does.
- kind=inner: Kusto.Language reports the outer schema, so the common columns
  (same name and type in every input, plus the withsource column) are
  selected in the translator; the evaluator drops the other columns instead
  of failing.
- isfuzzy=true: a name that resolves to no table is skipped. Kusto.Language
  reports it as warning KS205, which no longer aborts the query.
- IRUnionOperatorNode can also apply an operator to the piped input before
  the union (used by search in the next commit).

Limit: withsource values are bare table names (no database prefix).
